The error "Failed to load the app" is caused by a mismatch between your Firebase configuration and your service code.

*   **`services/firebase.ts`** is initializing Firebase using the **Compatibility (v8)** syntax (`firebase.firestore()`).
*   **`services/authService.ts`** and **`services/globalFeedbackService.ts`** are attempting to use the **Modular (v9)** syntax (e.g., `createUserWithEmailAndPassword(auth, ...)`, `doc(db, ...)`).

You cannot pass a "Compatibility" database instance to "Modular" functions. This causes the app to crash immediately upon loading.

I will fix this by reverting the service files to use the **Compatibility syntax**, which aligns with your existing `firebase.ts` and `CollaborativeSession.tsx`.

